Let  $P(i) = f(i)+f(43+i)+f(2\cdot43+i)+\cdots+f(46\cdot43+i)$ . Then,  $P(i) = (-2)^i$  for all  $0 \leq i \leq 42$ . Notice,
\[ P(43) - P(0) = f(2021) - f(0). \]
By Lagrange Interpolation,
\begin{align*}
P(43) &= \sum_{i = 0}^{42} (-2)^i \cdot \dfrac{\prod_{j \neq i} (43-j)}{\prod_{j \neq i} (i-j)} 
&= \sum_{i = 0}^{42} (-2)^i \cdot \dfrac{43! / (43-i)}{i! \cdot (42-i)! \cdot (-1)^{42-i}} 
&= \sum_{i = 0}^{42} 2^i \cdot \dfrac{43!}{i! \cdot (43-i)!} 
&= \sum_{i = 0}^{42} 2^i \cdot \binom{43}{i} 
&= \left(\sum_{i = 0}^{43} 2^i \cdot \binom{43}{i}\right) - 2^{43}\cdot \binom{43}{43} 
&= 3^{42} - 2^{43}.
\end{align*}
But,  $P(0) = 1$ . Thus,  $f(2021)-f(0) = \boxed{3^{43}-2^{43}-1.}$

