Now we will prove that  $E$  cant have degree  $4,3,1$ .**Definition:**Given a sequence of non-negative integers  $d=(d_1\ge d_2\ge \dots \ge d_n)$ ,if there exist a graph among  $n$  vertices  $v_1,v_2\dots v_n$   such that each  $d_i$  is degree of some of the vertices,then the sequence   $d=(d_1\ge d_2\ge \dots \ge d_n)$  is called ***Degree Sequence.*****Theorem:**(*Havel-Hakimi*)  $d=(d_1\ge d_2\ge \dots \ge d_n)$  is a degree sequence if and only if   $$ d_2-1,d_3-1\dots,d_{d_1}-1,d_{d_1+1},\dots,d_n $$   is a degree sequence.
*proof.* See [Here](http://compalg.inf.elte.hu/~tony/Oktatas/TDK/FINAL/Chap%202.PDF)  $\square$ Now coming back to the main problem,observe any verticrs can have degree atmost 4.If  $E$  plays 4 games implies \begin{align}
(4,4,3,2,1) \text{is a degree sequence}
\iff (3,2,1,0) \text{is a degree sequence}
\iff (1,0) \text{is a degree sequence}
\end{align}
(3) is obviously false.
