<details><summary>Solution</summary>Note that each maximal run of cards with the same value that has length  $2, 3,$  and  $4$  contributes  $1, 1,$  and  $2,$  respectively to the number of times we have to remove cards. Therefore, by the Principle of Inclusion/Exclusion, we wish to find   $$ E_2-E_3+E_4, $$   where  $E_2, E_3,$  and  $E_4$  are the expected number of runs (not necessarily maximal) of cards with the same value of length  $2, 3,$  and  $4,$  respectively. By Linearity of Expectation, the answer is thus
\begin{align*}
11 \cdot \frac{3}{11} - 10 \cdot \frac{3}{11} \cdot \frac{2}{10} + 9 \cdot \frac{3}{11} \cdot \frac{2}{10} \cdot \frac{1}{9} &= 3 - \frac{6}{11} + \frac{3}{55} 
&= \boxed{\frac{138}{55}}.
\end{align*} $\square$</details>

